hiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"item\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"#elections\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"count\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1520014</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"delta\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"+25%\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> } ] }</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">GET /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/trending?scope=region:IN&#x26;window=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">5</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">m&#x26;k=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">20</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">&#x26;category=sports</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#B31D28;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#FDAEB7;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic\">...</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">POST /v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">/events                 </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// internal, batched</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"events\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: [ { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"item\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"#worldcup\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"region\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"IN\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"ts\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1731160800123</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"weight\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> },</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">              { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"item\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"#worldcup\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"region\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"US\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"ts\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1731160800150</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"weight\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> } ] }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">202</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> Accepted</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Events are sent by producers (app servers, clients through a collector) in batches of 100-1000 to cut overhead; <code>weight</code> lets a retweet count more than a view. The read API is cacheable: <code>Cache-Control: public, max-age=5</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Twitter's trends API and Google Trends expose a window + geo dimension; YouTube's trending tab is refreshed periodically, not per second.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A newsstand's \"best sellers this week\" sign, updated once in a while rather than after each sale.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Offering one endpoint per window as separate code paths instead of one parameterised query.</li>\n<li>No region/category dimension.</li>\n<li>Making the read API compute rankings on demand.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"estimates","title":"Estimates","html":"<p>Assume 1M events/s peak (about 300k/s average), 100M distinct items per day, K = 100.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Quantity</th>\n<th>Calculation</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Event size</td>\n<td>item id 16 B + region 2 B + ts 8 B + overhead</td>\n<td>~50 B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ingest bandwidth</td>\n<td>1M x 50 B</td>\n<td>50 MB/s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Raw event storage</td>\n<td>300k/s x 86,400 x 50 B</td>\n<td>~1.3 TB/day (keep a few days in Kafka/S3)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Exact counters</td>\n<td>100M items x (16 B key + 8 B count)</td>\n<td>~2.4 GB per window: fits in RAM, but update rate is high</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Windows</td>\n<td>1 min, 1 h, 24 h; per region (200)</td>\n<td>exact map per (window x region) explodes: ~600 maps</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Count-Min Sketch</td>\n<td>width 2^20 x depth 4 x 4 B counters</td>\n<td>16 MB per sketch, error under 0.0001 x total events</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kafka partitions</td>\n<td>1M msgs/s; a partition handles ~50-100k msgs/s</td>\n<td>20-30 partitions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Final result</td>\n<td>K=100 items x 50 B</td>\n<td>5 KB per (scope, window): trivial</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The input rate is the issue, not the output. Heavy hitters are few; the bulk of the 100M items appear once or twice and do not matter.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry example.</strong> Twitter/X reported processing hundreds of thousands of tweets per second at peak; trends are computed from streams (Storm/Heron lineage) with sketches.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Counting the crowd's cheers for each team with a few tally sheets, not an individual list for every spectator.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Estimating only the final answer's size.</li>\n<li>Using one hot Redis key for a counter at 1M/s.</li>\n<li>Not computing sketch sizes.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"high-level-design","title":"High-level design","html":"<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 1031.6000000000001 68\" width=\"1031.6000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Stream processing pipeline\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M419.6 34 L475.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M419.6 34 L475.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M708.4000000000001 34 L764.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M708.4000000000001 34 L764.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M860.4000000000001 34 L916.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M860.4000000000001 34 L916.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Producers</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"261.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"288.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Kafka (events, partition by item)</text><rect x=\"475.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"232.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"592\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Stream workers (local counts)</text><rect x=\"764.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"812.4000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Aggregator</text><rect x=\"916.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"968.0000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Top-K cache</text></svg><figcaption>Stream processing pipeline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 488.79999999999995 130\" width=\"488.79999999999995\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Read path\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M108 34 L164 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 34 L164 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M274.4 65 L330.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M274.4 65 L330.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M108 96 L330.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M108 96 L330.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">User</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Aggregator</text><rect x=\"164\" y=\"43\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"219.2\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Trending API</text><rect x=\"330.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"403.59999999999997\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis top-K cache</text></svg><figcaption>Read path</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Components:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Kafka</strong>: events partitioned by <code>hash(item)</code> so all events for one item land on one worker; no cross-worker double counting.</li>\n<li><strong>Stream workers</strong> (Flink, Kafka Streams, Spark Structured Streaming): each keeps a local Count-Min Sketch or exact map per window, and a min-heap of its local top K.</li>\n<li><strong>Aggregator</strong>: merges local heaps from all workers into the global top K every 1-5 s (since items are partitioned by hash, global top K is the top K of the union of local top K lists).</li>\n<li><strong>Top-K cache</strong>: Redis keys such as <code>trend:global:1h</code> storing a small JSON/ZSET, TTL 60 s.</li>\n<li><strong>Batch layer</strong> (optional): hourly Spark job computes exact counts from the raw log in S3 and corrects the speed layer.</li>\n<li><strong>Trending API</strong>: stateless, reads Redis, adds metadata (names, thumbnails).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity: partition by item, merge local top-K.</strong> Why: because each item lives on exactly one worker, local counts are exact (no merging counters) and merging K-lists is cheap. Alternative: partition by event round-robin and merge sketches (sketches add cell by cell), which balances load for hot items but needs more memory per worker and a bigger merge. Breaks with one mega hot item (a single partition gets 10% of traffic): split hot keys into sub-keys with random suffixes and sum later. Reversible by reprocessing from Kafka.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity: stream vs batch.</strong> Stream processing gives seconds of freshness. Batch-only (hourly MapReduce) is simple and exact but stale. Lambda architecture runs both: fast approximate now, corrected later. Kappa architecture uses only the stream with replay. Choose Kappa unless you need exact audited counts.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Twitter's trends pipeline, LinkedIn's trending, Netflix's Top 10 (batch daily), Uber's surge uses windows.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Each cashier keeps a tally of her own best sellers; the manager only compares the cashiers' short lists.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Computing the global top K by sorting all counters.</li>\n<li>Forgetting that top K of a union needs each worker's top K (not just top 1).</li>\n<li>No answer for a single dominating hot key.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"deep-dives","title":"Deep dives","html":"<h3>Counting windows</h3>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 626.8 68\" width=\"626.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sliding window made of small buckets\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 34 L346 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 34 L346 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Events</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">1-minute bucket</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"12\" width=\"268.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"480.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Sum last 60 buckets = 1-hour count</text></svg><figcaption>Sliding window made of small buckets</figcaption></figure>\n<p>A sliding window of 1 hour is built from 60 one-minute buckets. Every minute: add the newest bucket, subtract (drop) the oldest. Store counts per <code>(item, minuteBucket)</code>. For the 24 h window use 24 one-hour buckets (rolled up from minute buckets). Memory = items x buckets, so only track candidate heavy hitters rather than all 100M items. Tumbling windows (fixed, non-overlapping) are cheaper but show jumps at boundaries; Flink supports sliding windows natively.</p>\n<h3>Count-Min Sketch</h3>\n<p>A 2-D array of <code>d</code> rows by <code>w</code> columns of counters. To add an item, hash it with <code>d</code> hash functions and increment one cell per row. To estimate, take the minimum of its <code>d</code> cells (collisions only overestimate). Error: estimate &#x3C;= true + epsilon x N with probability 1 - delta, where <code>w = e/epsilon</code> and <code>d = ln(1/delta)</code>. With <code>w</code> = 2^20 and <code>d</code> = 4 the error is about 3 x 10^-6 x N; at N = 3.6 billion events/hour that is about 10,000 extra, negligible for items with millions of hits.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">import</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> heapq, mmh3   </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># mmh3 = MurmurHash3</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">class</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> CMS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> __init__</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(self, w</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">&#x3C;&#x3C;</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">20</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, d</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">4</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">        self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.w, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.d </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> w, d</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">        self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.t </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> [[</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">]</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">*</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">w </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">for</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> _ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">in</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> range</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(d)]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> add</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(self, x, c</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">        for</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> i </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">in</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> range</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.d):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">            self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.t[i][mmh3.hash(x, i) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">%</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.w] </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">+=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> c</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    def</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> est</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(self, x):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">        return</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> min</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.t[i][mmh3.hash(x, i) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">%</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.w] </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">for</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> i </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">in</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> range</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">self</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.d))</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 678.0000000000001 68\" width=\"678.0000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sketch plus heap tracks the heavy hitters\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M456.40000000000003 34 L512.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M456.40000000000003 34 L512.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Event</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Update sketch</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Estimate count</text><rect x=\"512.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"589.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Min-heap of size K</text></svg><figcaption>Sketch plus heap tracks the heavy hitters</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The sketch cannot list its keys, so pair it with a min-heap of size K: after each add, if the item's estimate beats the heap's smallest, insert it. Alternative: the <strong>Space-Saving</strong> algorithm keeps exactly <code>m</code> counters (for example 10,000) and evicts the smallest, giving guaranteed heavy-hitter detection with tiny memory. Decision gravity: sketch vs exact map: pick the sketch when memory per window matters and ranks need not be perfect; reversible by switching the worker implementation.</p>\n<h3>Trending is velocity, not volume</h3>\n<p>\"Top by count\" shows always-popular items (#love). To detect a surge, compare the current window to a baseline: <code>score = (current - expected) / sqrt(expected + 1)</code> (z-score style) or ratio <code>current / avg of same hour over last 7 days</code>. Twitter described novelty as part of trends. Keep a slow baseline sketch per item for the long window and a fast one for the recent window; the difference ranks \"rising\" items. Filter spam and blocklisted topics before publishing.</p>\n<h3>Merging and the hot key</h3>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 822 68\" width=\"822\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hot key splitting\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M172.8 34 L228.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M172.8 34 L228.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M404 34 L460 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M404 34 L460 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M664 34 L720 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M664 34 L720 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"92.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Event for #worldcup</text><rect x=\"228.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"175.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"316.40000000000003\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Add random suffix 0-9</text><rect x=\"460\" y=\"12\" width=\"204\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"562\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">10 sub-keys on 10 workers</text><rect x=\"720\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"765\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Merge sum</text></svg><figcaption>Hot key splitting</figcaption></figure>\n<p>When one item gets a huge share, salt its key into n sub-keys (<code>#worldcup#7</code>), count independently, then sum in the aggregator. Detect hot keys by sampling 1% of events.</p>\n<h3>Publishing results</h3>\n<p>Aggregator pushes the merged top K to Redis every 1-5 s as an atomic <code>RENAME</code> of a temp key (readers never see half a list). Add a \"last good\" fallback if the pipeline stalls. CDN-cache the API for 5 s so 100k user reads/s become a handful of origin hits.</p>\n<h3>Fault tolerance and exactly-once</h3>\n<p>Flink checkpoints state (sketches, heaps) to S3 every minute with Kafka offsets; on crash it restarts from the checkpoint and reprocesses: counts are consistent (exactly-once state semantics). Late events beyond the watermark (say 30 s) are dropped or sent to a correction batch. Replaying Kafka allows recomputation after a bug fix. Decision: event time vs processing time; event time with watermarks is correct for mobile clients that send late.</p>\n<h3>Dimensions: region and category</h3>\n<p>Add region/category to the key: <code>(region, item)</code>. Number of sketches = windows x regions. Compute global as the sum of regional sketches (sketches add cell-wise) instead of counting twice. Keep top-K per region only for the top 50 regions; the rest roll up.</p>\n<p><strong>Production incident patterns.</strong> (1) A single partition lagging because of a hot key: Kafka consumer lag on one partition; mitigate with key salting. (2) Trending list stuck for 10 minutes because the aggregator died: monitor <code>computedAt</code> age and alert at 30 s. (3) Spam campaigns hijacking trends: add distinct-user counting (HyperLogLog, 12 KB per item) so 10,000 posts from 5 accounts do not outrank 5,000 posts from 5,000 accounts.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Twitter/X trends, YouTube trending, Google Trends, Redis HyperLogLog (<code>PFADD</code>) for distinct users.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A bouncer counting how many different people walk in, not just how many times one person walks through the door.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Count-Min Sketch with no heap, so you cannot list items.</li>\n<li>Using processing time and getting wrong windows for late mobile events.</li>\n<li>Equating trending with raw popularity.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-interviewers-look-for","title":"What interviewers look for","html":"<ul>\n<li>Recognising this as streaming heavy-hitters, not a SQL group-by.</li>\n<li>Sliding windows built from buckets, and the memory trade-off.</li>\n<li>Count-Min Sketch or Space-Saving with a heap, with error reasoning.</li>\n<li>Merging local top-K lists after partitioning by item; hot-key salting.</li>\n<li>Distinguishing velocity from volume, and spam resistance (distinct users via HyperLogLog).</li>\n<li>Operational view: checkpoints, replay, freshness metric, cached read API.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Stream events into Kafka partitioned by item; workers keep windowed counts and local top-K heaps.</li>\n<li>A global aggregator merges the local lists every few seconds and writes a small result to Redis.</li>\n<li>Sliding windows are sums of small time buckets; trending uses growth relative to a baseline.</li>\n<li>Count-Min Sketch (16 MB) plus a min-heap, or Space-Saving, gives bounded error with tiny memory.</li>\n<li>Salt hot keys; use HyperLogLog for distinct users to resist spam.</li>\n<li>Checkpoint state and replay from Kafka for recovery; optionally correct with an hourly exact batch.</li>\n<li>The API only reads a precomputed, CDN-cacheable result.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}